  Sesame Robot - an open-source, 3D-printed, ESP32 quadruped with a face.
  Original design: Dorian Borian (https://github.com/dorianborian/sesame-robot)
  Hardware replication, circuit assembly, servo calibration and testing: Soham Kadu
  (repository used as the reference: soham0777/sesame-robot).

Derived material in this project (all prepared offline, changes stated):
  - Assets/Models/Sesame/*.glb : the printed-part meshes converted from the repo STL files
      Internal-Frame-v121, Bottom-Cover-v121, L1..L4-v117, R1..R4-v117, Top-Cover-Cat-v100.
    Changes: units millimetres -> glTF metres (shown in centimetres), axes re-oriented, mirrored/rotated into one
    assembly frame (placement is illustrative), re-centred on each part's joint pivot, a flat colour material added.
    No geometry was simplified or edited.
  - Assets/Scripts/WizFaces.ts : OLED face bitmaps extracted from firmware/face-bitmaps.h (unchanged pixels).
  - Assets/Scripts/ProjectPack.ts : servo pins/names, I2C pins/address, wiring and movement sequences transcribed
    from firmware/sesame-firmware-main.ino, firmware/movement-sequences.h, docs/wiring-guide and docs/build-guide.

Electronics models (Lolin S2 Mini, buck converter, battery, rocker switch, header strip, SSD1306 OLED, MG90S servo)
are built from primitives at standard sizes that are NOT from the repo; they are labelled as such in the app.

The Apache-2.0 licence text of the original project is available at the URL above and in the upstream repository
(LICENSE). Modified files carry this notice of change.

